+	 * rule_gum=0 (qos.c), i.e. NON-STICKY, and matches with -m connbytes, which
+	 * re-evaluates per packet -- incompatible with hardware flow offload. The
+	 * standing guidance since the v2 metal validation has been "classify on
+	 * port/proto/IP/MAC, never transferred bytes"; the shipped defaults were the
+	 * thing violating it. Every rule below carries an EMPTY transferred field.
+	 *
+	 * Note what is deliberately NOT here: a Streaming preset. Streaming video is
+	 * TCP/UDP 443, indistinguishable from web browsing by port -- which is exactly
+	 * why the old pack reached for byte counts. That class is meant to be filled
+	 * by per-device rules (the TV's MAC or IP), which are sticky and offload-safe.
+	 * 80/443 therefore sits in Web/VoIP: it carries interactive web AND the ACK
+	 * stream of every download, both of which want a short queue, and the
+	 * committed minimums on the lower classes (qos_minrates) keep a bulk HTTPS
+	 * upload in that class from starving them. */
+	{ "qos_rulelist", "<Conferencing>>3478:3481>udp>>0<SIP>>5060:5061>udp>>0<Game Console>>3074>udp>>1<Steam>>27015:27030>udp>>1<BitTorrent>>6881:6889>tcp/udp>>3<Web>>80,443>tcp/udp>>0", CKN_STR4096, CKN_TYPE_DEFAULT, CKN_ACC_LEVEL_DEFAULT, CKN_ENC_DEFAULT, 0 },
 
 	/* reaper 2026-08-11 (owner-set profile, replaces the v3 template):
 	 *   Q1 Web/VoIP  p   min 15  ceil 100
